IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- LAYER 1 -- Part 7 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds
-- (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692), United Kingdom: regs 61 to 64
-- (lines 2055-2094 of uksi-2017-692.txt).  The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THESE REGULATIONS DO.  Part 7 gives the funds transfer regulation (the EU rules on the
-- information that must accompany a transfer of funds) a UK supervisor: reg 62 says whether the
-- FCA or the Commissioners supervises a payment service provider for it, reg 63 puts on that
-- supervisor the same kind of duties reg 46 to 50 put on the supervisors of the Money Laundering
-- Regulations, and reg 64 makes a payment service provider able to answer enquiries from the
-- police and financial investigators.  The funds transfer regulation itself is not in the text.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER.  As in the other modules of this encoding: a function answers JUST TRUE,
-- JUST FALSE or NOTHING; NOTHING is "the Regulations do not answer on these facts" and is never
-- read as no.  A duty "must" not discharged, a flat negative, a "provided that", "if" or "where"
-- that fails, and a fixed period outside which the text says no, answer JUST FALSE; a scope limit
-- with no "only", a list that is not closed and an answer that belongs to another section answer
-- NOTHING.  Marginal readings (a), (b) and (c) are in NOTES.md.

§ `Part 7 -- Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations (regs 61 to 64)`

DECLARE `reg 63 act of an authority` IS ONE OF
    `reg 63(1)(a) monitor effectively the payment service providers`
    `reg 63(1)(b) take the measures necessary to secure compliance`
    `reg 63(1)(c) take effective measures to encourage the payment service provider to report breaches`
    `reg 63(1)(d) take such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate and co-ordinate`
    `reg 63(5) inform the NCA`

§§ `Regulation 61 -- Interpretation`

-- The facts about a payment service provider that reg 62 sorts on.
DECLARE `reg 62 payment service provider` HAS
    `a payment service provider`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `an authorised person`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `an authorised payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a registered small payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
    `included in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an authorised electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a registered small electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Regulation 62 -- Transfer of funds supervisory authorities`

-- src:2059 | (1) The FCA is the transfer of funds supervisory authority for payment service providers, who are—
-- src:2060 | (a) authorised persons;
-- src:2061 | (b) authorised payment institutions under the Payment Services Regulations 2017 which are not included in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 54(2);
-- src:2062 | (c) registered small payment institutions under the Payment Services Regulations 2017 which are not included in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 54(2);
-- src:2063 | (d) authorised electronic money institutions under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011 ; or
-- src:2064 | (e) registered small electronic money institutions under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011.
@ref reg 62(1) (src:2059-2064)
GIVEN provider IS A `reg 62 payment service provider`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 62(1) the FCA is the transfer of funds supervisory authority for the payment service provider` MEANS
    IF (NOT provider's `a payment service provider`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for payment service providers" -- a person who is not a payment service provider is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (provider's `an authorised person`
            OR (provider's `an authorised payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017` AND (NOT provider's `included in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)`))
            OR (provider's `a registered small payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017` AND (NOT provider's `included in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)`))
            OR provider's `an authorised electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011`
            OR provider's `a registered small electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The FCA is the transfer of funds supervisory authority for payment service providers, who are (a) to (e)" -- paragraph (2) and regulation 61 use these limbs as the test of who comes within paragraph (1), so for a payment service provider that is in none of them the answer is JUST FALSE (delegated reading (a) of 2026-11-05; fork F12)
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2065 | (2) The Commissioners are the transfer of funds supervisory authority for payment service providers who do not come within paragraph (1).
@ref reg 62(2) (src:2065)
GIVEN provider IS A `reg 62 payment service provider`
      `the payment service provider comes within paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 62(2) the Commissioners are the transfer of funds supervisory authority for the payment service provider` MEANS
    IF (NOT provider's `a payment service provider`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for payment service providers who do not come within paragraph (1)" -- a person who is not a payment service provider is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the payment service provider comes within paragraph (1)`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who do not come within paragraph (1)" -- one who does is outside the paragraph
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the provider comes within paragraph (1) is that paragraph's answer and it has not been given
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Paragraph (2) read straight from the provider's own limbs, with no hand-made input: "do not come
-- within paragraph (1)" is the answer of paragraph (1), which is now JUST FALSE for a payment
-- service provider outside its five limbs (fork F12).
@ref reg 62(2) (src:2065)
GIVEN provider IS A `reg 62 payment service provider`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 62(2) the Commissioners are the transfer of funds supervisory authority for the provider, read from the provider's own limbs` MEANS
    `reg 62(2) the Commissioners are the transfer of funds supervisory authority for the payment service provider` provider (`reg 62(1) the FCA is the transfer of funds supervisory authority for the payment service provider` provider)

-- Hand-gathered (ruling E1, option B as guidance): reg 61 says the supervisory authority "is the
-- supervisory authority specified by regulation 62", and regs 62(1) and 62(2) each specify one.
-- The function gathers the two answers into the authority.
-- src:2057 | In this Part “transfer of funds supervisory authority” in relation to a payment service provider means the supervisory authority specified by regulation 62.
@ref reg 61 (src:2057)
GIVEN `the answer of regulation 62(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of regulation 62(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Authority
`reg 61 the transfer of funds supervisory authority of the payment service provider` MEANS
    IF `the answer of regulation 62(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `the Financial Conduct Authority`
    ELSE IF `the answer of regulation 62(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither paragraph specifies an authority on the facts given, so the text names none
         ELSE NOTHING

-- The same definition read straight from the provider's own limbs: regulation 62(1) and (2) are
-- answered from the provider and gathered by the function above.
@ref reg 61 (src:2057)
GIVEN provider IS A `reg 62 payment service provider`
GIVETH A MAYBE Authority
`reg 61 the transfer of funds supervisory authority of the provider, read from the provider's own limbs` MEANS
    `reg 61 the transfer of funds supervisory authority of the payment service provider` (`reg 62(1) the FCA is the transfer of funds supervisory authority for the payment service provider` provider) (`reg 62(2) the Commissioners are the transfer of funds supervisory authority for the provider, read from the provider's own limbs` provider)

§§ `Regulation 63 -- Duties of transfer of funds supervisory authorities`

-- The duties of reg 63(1) fall on the authority that is the transfer of funds supervisory
-- authority "for" the payment service providers: reg 61's answer names it.
-- src:2067 | (1) A transfer of funds supervisory authority must—
@ref reg 63(1) (src:2067)
GIVEN `reg 61 the transfer of funds supervisory authority of the payment service provider` IS A MAYBE Authority
      `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 63(1) the authority is a transfer of funds supervisory authority for the payment service provider` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 61 the transfer of funds supervisory authority of the payment service provider`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who the supervisory authority is, is reg 62's answer and it has not been given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST named THEN
        IF named EQUALS `the authority`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A transfer of funds supervisory authority must" -- another authority is outside the paragraph
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2067 | (1) A transfer of funds supervisory authority must—
-- src:2068 | (a) monitor effectively the payment service providers for whom it is the transfer of funds supervisory authority;
@ref reg 63(1)(a) (src:2067-2068)
GIVEN `it has monitored effectively the payment service providers for whom it is the transfer of funds supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 63(1)(a) the authority has monitored effectively the payment service providers` MEANS
    IF `it has monitored effectively the payment service providers for whom it is the transfer of funds supervisory authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must monitor effectively" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 63(1)(a) (src:2068)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 63 act of an authority`
`reg 63(1)(a) the authority must monitor effectively the payment service providers (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 63(1)(a) monitor effectively the payment service providers`

-- src:2067 | (1) A transfer of funds supervisory authority must—
-- src:2069 | (b) take the measures necessary to secure compliance by payment service providers with the requirements of the funds transfer regulation;
@ref reg 63(1)(b) (src:2067-2069)
GIVEN `it has taken the measures necessary to secure compliance by payment service providers with the requirements of the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 63(1)(b) the authority has taken the measures necessary to secure compliance` MEANS
    IF `it has taken the measures necessary to secure compliance by payment service providers with the requirements of the funds transfer regulation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must take the measures necessary" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 63(1)(b) (src:2069)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 63 act of an authority`
`reg 63(1)(b) the authority must take the measures necessary to secure compliance (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 63(1)(b) take the measures necessary to secure compliance`

-- src:2067 | (1) A transfer of funds supervisory authority must—
-- src:2070 | (c) take effective measures to encourage the payment service provider to report breaches of the provisions of the funds transfer regulation to the authority;
@ref reg 63(1)(c) (src:2067-2070)
GIVEN `it has taken effective measures to encourage the payment service provider to report breaches of the provisions of the funds transfer regulation to the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 63(1)(c) the authority has taken effective measures to encourage the payment service provider to report breaches` MEANS
    IF `it has taken effective measures to encourage the payment service provider to report breaches of the provisions of the funds transfer regulation to the authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must take effective measures" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 63(1)(c) (src:2070)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 63 act of an authority`
`reg 63(1)(c) the authority must take effective measures to encourage reporting of breaches (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 63(1)(c) take effective measures to encourage the payment service provider to report breaches`

-- "(d) take such steps as it considers appropriate (i) to co-operate with other supervisory
-- authorities, the Treasury and law enforcement authorities ...; (ii) to co-ordinate activities
-- ...; (iii) to co-operate with overseas authorities to ensure the effective supervision of a
-- payment service provider to which paragraph (2) applies."  What the authority considers
-- appropriate is its own judgement, so each limb is a plain input.
-- src:2067 | (1) A transfer of funds supervisory authority must—
-- src:2071 | (d) take such steps as it considers appropriate—
-- src:2072 | (i) to co-operate with other supervisory authorities, the Treasury and law enforcement authorities in relation to the development and implementation of policies to counter money laundering and terrorist financing;
-- src:2073 | (ii) to co-ordinate activities to counter money laundering and terrorist financing;
-- src:2074 | (iii) to co-operate with overseas authorities to ensure the effective supervision of a payment service provider to which paragraph (2) applies.
@ref reg 63(1)(d) (src:2067-2074)
GIVEN `it has taken such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with other supervisory authorities, the Treasury and law enforcement authorities in relation to the development and implementation of policies to counter money laundering and terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken such steps as it considers appropriate to co-ordinate activities to counter money laundering and terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with overseas authorities to ensure the effective supervision of a payment service provider to which paragraph (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 63(1)(d) the authority has taken the steps it considers appropriate to co-operate and co-ordinate` MEANS
    IF `it has taken such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with other supervisory authorities, the Treasury and law enforcement authorities in relation to the development and implementation of policies to counter money laundering and terrorist financing`
       AND `it has taken such steps as it considers appropriate to co-ordinate activities to counter money laundering and terrorist financing`
       AND `it has taken such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with overseas authorities to ensure the effective supervision of a payment service provider to which paragraph (2) applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must take such steps as it considers appropriate" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 63(1)(d) (src:2071)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 63 act of an authority`
`reg 63(1)(d) the authority must take the steps it considers appropriate (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 63(1)(d) take such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate and co-ordinate`

-- src:2075 | (2) This paragraph applies to a payment service provider established—
-- src:2076 | (a) in the United Kingdom, which has its head office in another country; or
-- src:2077 | (b) in another country but which has its head office in the United Kingdom.
@ref reg 63(2) (src:2075-2077)
GIVEN `the payment service provider is established in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment service provider has its head office in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 63(2) paragraph (2) applies to the payment service provider` MEANS
    IF `the payment service provider is established in the United Kingdom` AND (NOT `the payment service provider has its head office in the United Kingdom`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT `the payment service provider is established in the United Kingdom`) AND `the payment service provider has its head office in the United Kingdom`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): (a) and (b) say two cases to which the paragraph applies and do not say that it applies to no other
         ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2078 | (3) Co-operation may include the sharing of information which the supervisory authority is not prevented from disclosing.
@ref reg 63(3) (src:2078)
GIVEN `it is information which the supervisory authority is not prevented from disclosing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 63(3) co-operation may include the sharing of the information` MEANS
    IF `it is information which the supervisory authority is not prevented from disclosing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the sharing of information which the supervisory authority is not prevented from disclosing" -- information it is prevented from disclosing is outside the permission
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Reg 63(4) is a line of dots in this rendering: text removed; nothing is encoded.

-- src:2080 | (5) A transfer of funds supervisory authority which, in the course of carrying out any of its functions under this Part or otherwise, knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a payment service provider is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing must as soon as practicable inform the NCA.
@ref reg 63(5) (src:2080)
GIVEN `it knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a payment service provider is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 63(5) the authority must inform the NCA` MEANS
    IF `it knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a payment service provider is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A transfer of funds supervisory authority which ... knows or suspects" is a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "as soon as practicable" is a period the text leaves to judgement, so it is a plain input.
@ref reg 63(5) (src:2080)
GIVEN `it knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a payment service provider is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has informed the NCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it informed the NCA as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 63(5) the authority has informed the NCA as soon as practicable` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a payment service provider is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A transfer of funds supervisory authority which ... knows or suspects" is a scope limit with no "only"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it has informed the NCA` AND `it informed the NCA as soon as practicable`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must as soon as practicable inform the NCA" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 63(5) (src:2080)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 63 act of an authority`
`reg 63(5) the authority must inform the NCA (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY `the authority`
    MUST `reg 63(5) inform the NCA`

-- src:2081 | (6) A disclosure made under paragraph (5) is not to be taken to breach any restriction, however imposed, on the disclosure of information.
@ref reg 63(6) (src:2081)
GIVEN `the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 63(6) the disclosure is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A disclosure made under paragraph (5)" -- a disclosure made otherwise is outside the protection
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2082 | (7) Where a disclosure under paragraph (5) is made in good faith, no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person by whom, or or on whose behalf, it is made.
@ref reg 63(7) (src:2082)
GIVEN `the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 63(7) no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person who made it` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)` AND `it was made in good faith`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a disclosure under paragraph (5) is made in good faith" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2083 | (8) The functions of the FCA under this Part are to be treated for the purposes of section 1A of, and Parts 1, 2 and 4 of Schedule 1ZA to, FSMA (the Financial Conduct Authority) as functions conferred on the FCA under that Act.
@ref reg 63(8) (src:2083)
GIVEN `it is a function of the FCA under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
