    ELSE NOTHING

-- Reg 63(9) is a line of dots in this rendering: text removed; nothing is encoded.
-- Reg 63(10).  As in reg 50(4), the "and" joins two kinds of authority and a body is an overseas
-- authority if it is either (fork F2).
-- src:2085 | (10) For the purposes of this regulation, “overseas authority” means—
-- src:2086 | (a) an authority responsible for any of the functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation in an EEA state ... in which the payment service provider is established or has its head office; and
-- src:2087 | (b) where the payment service provider is established or has its head office in another country which is not an EEA state, an authority in that country which has equivalent functions to any of the functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation.
@ref reg 63(10) (src:2085-2087)
GIVEN `the body is responsible for any of the functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is in an EEA state in which the payment service provider is established or has its head office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment service provider is established or has its head office in another country which is not an EEA state` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is in that country and has functions equivalent to any of the functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 63(10) the body is an overseas authority` MEANS
    IF `the body is responsible for any of the functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation`
       AND `the body is in an EEA state in which the payment service provider is established or has its head office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the payment service provider is established or has its head office in another country which is not an EEA state`
            AND `the body is in that country and has functions equivalent to any of the functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means" -- neither (a) nor (b) is met
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 64 -- Obligations of payment service providers`

-- Reg 64(1) is a line of dots in this rendering: text removed; nothing is encoded.
-- Reg 64(3): the persons who may ask.  The accreditation under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 is
-- that Act's, which is not staged here, so the accreditation and the acting for the Scottish
-- Ministers are plain facts about the enquirer (a named input, not an answer from another section).
-- src:2091 | (3) The persons specified in this paragraph are—
-- src:2092 | (a) financial investigators accredited under section 3 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (accreditation and training) ;
-- src:2093 | (b) persons acting on behalf of the Scottish Ministers in their capacity as an enforcement authority under that Act; and
-- src:2094 | (c) constables or equivalent officers of any law enforcement authority.
@ref reg 64(3) (src:2091-2094)
GIVEN `the person is a financial investigator accredited under section 3 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is acting on behalf of the Scottish Ministers in their capacity as an enforcement authority under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a constable or an equivalent officer of any law enforcement authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64(3) the person is a person specified in this paragraph` MEANS
    IF `the person is a financial investigator accredited under section 3 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002`
       OR `the person is acting on behalf of the Scottish Ministers in their capacity as an enforcement authority under that Act`
       OR `the person is a constable or an equivalent officer of any law enforcement authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The persons specified in this paragraph are" -- the person is none of (a) to (c)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The rendering shows "..." after "able" in (2): text removed there.
-- src:2090 | (2) A payment service provider must ensure that it is able ... to respond fully and rapidly to enquiries from a person specified in paragraph (3) concerning any of the information required by or under the funds transfer regulation.
@ref reg 64(2) (src:2090)
GIVEN `the person making the enquiry is a person specified in paragraph (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the enquiry concerns information required by or under the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment service provider is able to respond fully and rapidly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 64(2) the payment service provider is able to respond fully and rapidly to the enquiry` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person making the enquiry is a person specified in paragraph (3)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the enquirer is a person specified in paragraph (3) is that paragraph's answer and it has not been given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "enquiries from a person specified in paragraph (3)" -- an enquiry from another person is outside the paragraph
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (NOT `the enquiry concerns information required by or under the funds transfer regulation`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "enquiries ... concerning any of the information required by or under the funds transfer regulation" -- an enquiry about other information is outside the paragraph
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF `the payment service provider is able to respond fully and rapidly`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ensure that it is able ... to respond fully and rapidly" (Marginal readings, (c))
             ELSE JUST FALSE
